# Build-context trim for deploy/Dockerfile.backend (T-11).
#
# The build context is the repo root (`..` from this file — see
# deploy/docker-compose.yml's `build.context`) because the backend image
# needs pyproject.toml/uv.lock (repo root) AND backend/src/** AND
# fixtures/** (the seed data `data.seed.seed_all` reads at container
# start — see deploy/backend/bootstrap.py). BuildKit honors a
# `<Dockerfile-name>.dockerignore` file colocated with the Dockerfile
# itself (verified against this Docker install), so this trims the
# context without needing a root-level .dockerignore, which is outside
# T-11's edit scope (backend/**, portal/**, and root files belong to
# other tickets).
#
# Everything not listed here IS sent to the daemon — this is an
# exclude-list, not an include-list. An earlier `* ` + `!keep/me`
# include-list approach was tried and discarded: dockerignore (like
# gitignore) cannot re-include a path whose parent directory was already
# excluded by a broader pattern, so `*` followed by `!backend/src` sends
# nothing. Enumerating what NOT to send avoids that trap.
.claude
.codegraph
.deepeval
.env
.env.local
.git
.github
.gitignore
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.venv
CLAUDE.md
README.md
backend/tests
docker-compose.yml
docs
evals
portal
promptfooconfig.yaml
scripts
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.DS_Store
